From: Daniel <daniel@teide.tech>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 18:14:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 04/13] Controller screens: native Kontrol S8 frame encoder
 (transform="s8:N")

The QML transformFrame runs on the controller thread, the same thread that
handles HID input, so screen encoding in JS (~2 ms/frame, 40 frames/s) held
fader and button input up. With <screen transform="s8:0"> frames are
encoded in C++ instead (~22 us), sending only changed pixel pairs (skip
runs) plus a full frame every 150 frames.

Also: with --controller-debug every transformed frame was sent twice.
